+// `tensor_content` of a mangled TensorProto (e.g. the payload of
+// #tf_type<tensor_proto : "...">) is always stored in little-endian byte
+// order, so that MLIR text and bytecode containing such attributes mean the
+// same thing on every host. In memory, TensorProto::tensor_content follows the
+// TensorFlow convention of host byte order, so on big-endian hosts the bytes
+// are swapped when mangling and demangling. On little-endian hosts this is a
+// no-op.
+bool NeedsByteSwap(const TensorProto& tensor) {
+  return !port::kLittleEndian && !tensor.tensor_content().empty() &&
